data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"\"content\": \"# Campaign hello2952 — final summary (orchestrator)\\n\\n## Outcome: campaign-met\\n\\nA served interface is live on `0.0.0.0:5173` (Vite dev server, left running),\\nshowing the greeting \\\"Hello, world!\\\" whose colour the viewer changes with\\nthree buttons (Blue / Orange / Violet), built entirely from the\\n`@codesweep-ai/ui` design system.\\n\\n## What was delivered\\n\\nOrchestrator branch `cs-sandbox/<ORCHESTRATOR:1>.<GROUP:1>`,\\nHEAD `871270f` (\\\"Implement Colour Greeting page per DESIGN.md\\\"), differs from\\nbase `4f159b9`:\\n\\n- `DESIGN.md` (orchestrator, commit `3cd2423`) — the design both agents worked\\n  from: greeting text, three token colours (`--color-cat-1` / `--color-cat-6`\\n  / `--color-cat-5`, default Blue), AppShell + Header (\\\"Colour Greeting\\\", no\\n  nav) + Footer (\\\"Built with the codesweep design system\\\") + Button\\n  (secondary/md), centred layout, `useState` behaviour.\\n- The application (developer, commit `871270f`, fast-forwarded into my\\n  branch): React 19 + Vite, `@codesweep-ai/ui ^0.3.0`, token-only colours (no\\n  hex anywhere), style sheets imported once at the entry point, dev server\\n  bound to 0.0.0.0:5173, `.gitignore` (node_modules/, dist/), README\\n  documenting `npm run build` and `npm run serve`.\\n\\n## How it was held to the design\\n\\n- Orchestrator's own check: fetched and merged the developer's branch, read\\n  every source file against DESIGN.md, `npm run build` passed, started the dev\\n  server (0.0.0.0:5173, still running), confirmed the page serves HTTP 200\\n  with the greeting, the three tokens and the DS components, and that the DS\\n  package renders `data-component` attributes.\\n- qa verification (d002, accepted): PASS on every requirement, measured with\\n  headless Chromium against the production build — exact greeting, button\\n  labels, computed greeting colour after real clicks (`rgb(111,147,201)` /\\n  `rgb(216,146,89)` / `rgb(158,144,204)` = the three token values), centred\\n  layout geometry, `data-component` attributes for AppShell/Header/Footer/\\n  Button, no hex values in source. qa's report:\\n  `~/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/` (qa side) — verdict PASS, no failures.\\n\\n## Campaign course\\n\\n- d001: briefing confirmed by all members.\\n- developer d002: implemented per design; accepted after my own verification.\\n- qa d002: verified per design; accepted. No rework cycles were needed.\\n\\n## Unmet items\\n\\nNone. Every stated criterion is satisfied: the interface is designed, built\\nfrom the design system (Header, Footer, Button, colour tokens), verified\\nagainst the design, and served on 0.0.0.0 port 5173, left running.\\n"},"index":0}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1793344063,"id":"chatcmpl-4d91d413","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

